<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 1386) <span class="when">Oct 10, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li>Small improvements to the Review Manager.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1382) <span class="when">Oct 10, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>The Review Manager</b> groups reviews by project and sorts them (Active, Newest, Name and more). Showcases carry a yellow pill.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1367) <span class="when">Oct 10, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Join with your link.</b> Paste the link you were sent into <i>Review ▸ Join a Review…</i> or onto the lock screen. Invite files are no longer used, and the lock screen offers <i>Open License…</i> for a license file.</li>
<li>If your host watermarks your copy, your name is tiled faintly across the picture.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1360) <span class="when">Oct 9, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>The Review Manager</b> lists your reviews under a Reviews section, and opens on the review you came from.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1357) <span class="when">Oct 9, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>A simpler Review menu.</b> <i>Start a Review…</i> becomes <i>Review Window</i> once one is running (⇧⌘R), and <i>Join a Review…</i> is ⇧⌘J. Joining another review asks before it leaves the one you're in.</li>
<li><b>Leave Review keeps your access.</b> Leaving a review no longer resets you to the basic tier. <i>Sign Out of Asobi Review</i> is in the Asobi menu.</li>
<li><b>Open several things at once.</b> Open Media takes several files and whole folders, and folders bring in their movies and sequences only.</li>
<li><b>Buttons answer the click.</b> Every button shows when it's pressed, and slow ones spin until they're done.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1344) <span class="when">Oct 6, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li>Frame numbers and timecode in a review now match the studio's, so a clip that starts at 1001 reads 1001 here too.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1340) <span class="when">Oct 5, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li>Movies show their real frame numbers when the file says what they are; otherwise they start at 1. Playback ▸ First Frame Number… sets one if you need to.</li>
<li>The review page: click the timecode to switch to frame numbers.</li>
<li>Playlist: the line joining a pair switches its compare off and on.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1311) <span class="when">Oct 4, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li>Fixed: ending a compare from the review page now clears it here too.</li>
<li>Playlist: click the line joining a pair to clear its compare. The pair stays.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
